@startuml register-with-google
title Complete passwordless registration through Google
hide footbox

actor User
participant "CRM client" as Client
participant RegisterWithGoogleController as Controller
participant RegisterWithGoogleHandler as Handler
participant LoginSessionIssuer as Session
database "SQL Server" as Database

note over User,Client: Google sign-in returned registrationRequired
User -> Client: Submit role and profile details
Client -> Controller: POST /api/auth/google/register\n{continuationToken, role, userName, ...}
Controller -> Handler: Send RegisterWithGoogleCommand with request metadata\nvia MediatR
Handler -> Handler: Validate public role and hash continuation token
Handler -> Database: Begin transaction\nLookup by token hash with null AccountId and valid expiry
break No valid registration continuation
    Handler -> Database: Transaction rolls back
    Controller --> Client: 401 Auth.InvalidGoogleRegistrationContinuation
end
Handler -> Database: ExecuteDeleteAsync by token hash
Database --> Handler: Affected row count
break Another request consumed the continuation
    Handler -> Database: Transaction rolls back
    Controller --> Client: 401 Auth.InvalidGoogleRegistrationContinuation
end
Handler -> Database: Check email, Google subject, username\nand optional phone number for conflicts
break Email or profile data conflicts
    Handler -> Database: Transaction rolls back
    Controller --> Client: 409 ProblemDetails
end
Handler -> Handler: Create active UserAccount without a password\nUse verified email from continuation
alt Tutor selected
    Handler -> Handler: Assign Tutor role and stage Tutor record
else Student selected
    Handler -> Handler: Assign Student role and stage Student record
end
Handler -> Handler: Stage Google subject to CRM account link
Handler -> Session: Issue(account, request metadata)
Session --> Handler: CRM JWT and refresh token\nRefresh token hash staged for save
Handler -> Database: SaveChangesAsync for account, role, profile, link and session
break Unique constraint conflict on email or Google subject
    Handler -> Database: Transaction rolls back
    Controller --> Client: 409 Auth.GoogleRegistrationConflict
end
Handler -> Database: Commit all writes and continuation deletion
Handler --> Controller: LoginHandlerResult
opt Browser session
    Controller -> Controller: Append refresh cookie with LoginRefreshTokenCookie
end
Controller --> Client: 201 signedIn + CRM session\nNative mode includes refresh fields in JSON
@enduml
